{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "83ccf853-e454-558c-becb-ba0533a6070e",
    "name": "Investor API",
    "description": "Investor Negotiation Game API (local development).\n\n1. Import this collection and `local.postman_environment.json`, then select the **Investor local** environment.\n2. Start the API (`pnpm dev`, or `THINKING_PROVIDER=fake DECISION_PROVIDER=fake pnpm dev` without Ollama/laya-serve).\n3. Run **Session & CSRF** first (or run the whole collection in order with the Collection Runner).\n\nEvery response is checked for the security headers and, for errors, the `{ error: { code, message, requestId } }` envelope.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Runs after every request in the collection.",
          "pm.test('security headers', () => {",
          "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('X-Content-Type-Options')).to.eql('nosniff');",
          "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.has('X-Powered-By')).to.be.false;",
          "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('X-Request-Id')).to.match(/^[0-9a-f-]{36}$/);",
          "});",
          "if (pm.response.code >= 400) {",
          "  pm.test('error envelope', () => {",
          "    const { error } = pm.response.json();",
          "    pm.expect(error.code).to.match(/^[A-Z_]+$/);",
          "    pm.expect(error.message).to.be.a('string');",
          "    pm.expect(error.requestId).to.eql(pm.response.headers.get('X-Request-Id'));",
          "    pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.not.include('    at ');",
          "  });",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3001",
      "description": "Fallback when no environment is selected"
    },
    {
      "key": "allowedOrigin",
      "value": "http://localhost:5173"
    },
    {
      "key": "csrfToken",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Set by \"Get CSRF token\" (empty when CSRF is disabled)"
    },
    {
      "key": "csrfEnabled",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Set by \"Get CSRF token\": \"true\" or \"false\""
    },
    {
      "key": "playerId",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Set by \"Get session\""
    },
    {
      "key": "personaId",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Set by \"List personas\" (the first persona's id), for the game endpoints"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "id": "f4c57b70-6766-5e55-ac50-45d206f886c7",
      "name": "System",
      "description": "Liveness and provider reachability. No session or CSRF token needed.",
      "item": [
        {
          "id": "d0cdce48-111f-5527-a388-500cb0d07180",
          "name": "Health",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('status ok', () => pm.expect(body.status).to.eql('ok'));",
                  "pm.test('checks database/thinking/decision', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.checks).to.have.all.keys('database', 'thinking', 'decision');",
                  "  Object.values(body.checks).forEach((v) => pm.expect(v).to.be.oneOf(['ok', 'error']));",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('no provider identity leaked', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.not.match(/ollama|anthropic|laya|jev|llama|claude|https?:/i);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('no session cookie issued', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.has('Set-Cookie')).to.be.false);",
                  "if (body.checks.thinking === 'error' || body.checks.decision === 'error') {",
                  "  console.warn('A provider is unreachable: playground requests to it will fail.', body.checks);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/health",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "health"]
            },
            "description": "Database check decides 200/503. `checks.thinking` / `checks.decision` report the active LLM providers (cached ~30 s) and never change the status code."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "396c2fb6-8d9f-5b40-9b50-4fa626ab6d40",
      "name": "Session & CSRF",
      "description": "Run these first. Postman keeps the `inv.pid` player cookie for the host. When the server has CSRF enabled (`security.csrf.enabled` / `CSRF_ENABLED=true`), the token is saved to `csrfToken` and sent as `X-CSRF-Token` on every POST; it is bound to the player cookie, so after clearing cookies run \"Get CSRF token\" again. With CSRF disabled (the default) the token request answers 404 and no token is needed.",
      "item": [
        {
          "id": "9b8d8fc1-777d-5416-beb5-352b9dbae079",
          "name": "Get session",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('playerId is a UUID', () => pm.expect(body.playerId).to.match(/^[0-9a-f-]{36}$/));",
                  "pm.test('only public fields', () => pm.expect(body).to.have.all.keys('playerId', 'createdAt'));",
                  "const previous = pm.collectionVariables.get('playerId');",
                  "if (previous) pm.test('same player as before (cookie kept)', () => pm.expect(body.playerId).to.eql(previous));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('playerId', body.playerId);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/session",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "session"]
            },
            "description": "Creates the anonymous player on first call."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "id": "a94df01e-2856-5917-ab4c-9356bde7e2d6",
          "name": "Get CSRF token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 404) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('csrfEnabled', 'false');",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('csrfToken', '');",
                  "  pm.test('CSRF protection is disabled on this server (no token needed)', () => {});",
                  "} else {",
                  "  pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "  const { csrfToken } = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.test('token returned', () => pm.expect(csrfToken).to.be.a('string').with.length.above(32));",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('csrfEnabled', 'true');",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('csrfToken', csrfToken);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/csrf-token",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "csrf-token"]
            },
            "description": "Returns 404 when `security.csrf.enabled` is false (the committed default): the collection then records `csrfEnabled=false` and skips the CSRF-specific checks."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "0d797ba8-a215-53eb-a568-cfca485270f7",
      "name": "Game",
      "item": [
        {
          "id": "f47d7a58-7652-5f9c-882e-b32e571a0700",
          "name": "List personas",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('six personas', () => pm.expect(body.personas).to.have.lengthOf(6));",
                  "pm.test('public fields only', () => body.personas.forEach((p) => pm.expect(p).to.have.all.keys('id', 'name', 'avatar', 'tagline', 'traits')));",
                  "pm.test('no hidden numbers', () => ['budget', 'minEquity', 'maxEquity', 'patience', 'personality', 'toneInstructions'].forEach((key) => pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.not.include(`\"${key}\"`)));",
                  "if (body.personas.length) pm.collectionVariables.set('personaId', body.personas[0].id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/personas",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "personas"]
            },
            "description": "The investors a player can choose from: public profiles only, never the hidden negotiation numbers."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "dcb8e6ec-3391-5b97-bdef-df80ed2e94da",
      "name": "Playground",
      "description": "Dev-only endpoints (`dev.playground: true`, never in production) that call the **active** providers. With fake providers, `thinking/json` answers 502 (the fake has no scripted JSON). Mutations are rate-limited (60 per 15 min by default).",
      "item": [
        {
          "id": "3f77f91d-d0fb-56e5-b21e-fea43bf85e86",
          "name": "Thinking: text",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.collectionVariables.get('csrfEnabled') !== 'false' && !pm.collectionVariables.get('csrfToken')) {",
                  "  console.warn('csrfToken is empty: run \"Session & CSRF / Get CSRF token\" first.');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 503 || pm.response.code === 502) {",
                  "  console.warn('Provider error ' + pm.response.json().error.code +",
                  "    ': is the active provider running? Check GET /api/health and the server log.');",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('text reply', () => pm.expect(body.text).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);",
                  "pm.test('provider metadata', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.provider).to.be.oneOf(['ollama', 'anthropic', 'fake']);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.model).to.be.a('string');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.latencyMs).to.be.a('number');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-CSRF-Token",
                "value": "{{csrfToken}}",
                "description": "From \"Get CSRF token\""
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/dev/thinking/text",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "dev", "thinking", "text"]
            },
            "description": "",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"system\": \"You are a greedy, impatient startup investor. Reply in one or two short sentences.\",\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": \"I want €500k for 15% of my EV charging startup.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "id": "334a5415-20a5-57cb-8f19-2ab398ba230c",
          "name": "Thinking: JSON (reply options)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.collectionVariables.get('csrfEnabled') !== 'false' && !pm.collectionVariables.get('csrfToken')) {",
                  "  console.warn('csrfToken is empty: run \"Session & CSRF / Get CSRF token\" first.');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 503 || pm.response.code === 502) {",
                  "  console.warn('Provider error ' + pm.response.json().error.code +",
                  "    ': is the active provider running? Check GET /api/health and the server log.');",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "// `data` is a reserved sandbox global (iteration data), hence `generated`.",
                  "const generated = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "pm.test('data matches the posted schema', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(generated.options).to.be.an('array').that.is.not.empty;",
